{"step_index":83,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T06:01:27Z","input_tokens":2947,"cache_read_tokens":218066,"output_tokens":2266,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe plan is to add a helper function for creating panel boxes within the environment configuration file, ensuring consistent UV mapping and edge material application for various visual elements. This involves modifying material definitions, adjusting road, grass, skid, and sausage material properties, as well as applying specific image textures. The modifications include adjustments to specular IOR levels, emission values, and coat weight to refine the visual representation of different materials like asphalt, grass, skids, sausages, and the car material.\n\n\nAdjusting material definitions based on observed properties. Specifically, modifying specular IOR, emission strength, and coat weight for materials like asphalt, grass, skids, and car components for visual refinement. Focused on ensuring the correct textures and parameters for tire materials, including tire compound, sidewall, and specific visual separation for tread versus shoulder.\n\nCreated a dedicated material for the rain light to ensure it doesn't share parameters with other elements. Enhancing the appearance of carbon-ceramic brake discs using a color ramp for the emission color to achieve a glowing swept-annulus effect.\n\n\nFocused on refining the brake disc glow effect by ensuring compatibility with existing animation scripts. Confirmed the current node setup for `Mat_Brake_HeatGlow` is optimal for automated keyframe injection, allowing for dynamic emission adjustments. Considering the preview setup; will verify car positioning and camera configurations in the scratch verification script.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\pipeline\\v5_env.py","Replacement":"def box(name, center, size, mat, rot_z=0.0, up=False):\n    bm = bmesh.new()\n    bmesh.ops.create_cube(bm, size=1.0)\n    bmesh.ops.scale(bm, vec=size, verts=bm.verts)\n    me = bpy.data.meshes.new(name)\n    bm.to_mesh(me)\n    bm.free()\n    ob = bpy.data.objects.new(name, me)\n    COLL.objects.link(ob)\n    ob.location = center\n    ob.rotation_euler = (0, 0, rot_z)\n    me.materials.append(mat)\n    return ob\n\n\ndef panel_box(name, center, size, mat, rot_z=0.0, u_range=(0.0, 1.0), edge_mat=None):\n    \"\"\"带正确正立 UV 的双面展板盒：±Y 宽面贴图 mat（UV [u0..u1]x[0..1]），四条窄边用 edge_mat。\"\"\"\n    hx, hy, hz = size[0] / 2.0, size[1] / 2.0, size[2] / 2.0\n    verts = [\n        (-hx, -hy, -hz), (hx, -hy, -hz), (hx, -hy, hz), (-hx, -hy, hz),   # 0..3: -Y 面\n        (hx, hy, -hz), (-hx, hy, -hz), (-hx, hy, hz), (hx, hy, hz),       # 4..7: +Y 面\n    ]\n    faces = [\n        (0, 1, 2, 3),   # -Y 正面\n        (4, 5, 6, 7),   # +Y 背面\n        (1, 4, 7, 2),   # +X 侧边\n        (5, 0, 3, 6),   # -X 侧边\n        (3, 2, 7, 6),   # +Z 顶边\n        (5, 4, 1, 0),   # -Z 底边\n    ]\n    me = bpy.data.meshes.new(name)\n    me.from_pydata(verts, [], faces)\n    me.validate()\n    me.update()\n    ob = bpy.data.objects.new(name, me)\n    COLL.objects.link(ob)\n    ob.location = center\n    ob.rotation_euler = (0, 0, rot_z)\n    me.materials.append(mat)\n    emat = edge_mat or mat\n    if emat != mat:\n        me.materials.append(emat)\n    u0, u1 = u_range\n    uv_layer = me.uv_layers.new(name=\"UVMap\")\n    quad_uv = [(u0, 0.0), (u1, 0.0), (u1, 1.0), (u0, 1.0)]\n    for pi, poly in enumerate(me.polygons):\n        poly.material_index = 0 if pi < 2 else (1 if emat != mat else 0)\n        for k, li in enumerate(poly.loop_indices):\n            uv_layer.data[li].uv = quad_uv[k % 4]\n    return ob","Target":"def box(name, center, size, mat, rot_z=0.0, up=False):\n    bm = bmesh.new()\n    bmesh.ops.create_cube(bm, size=1.0)\n    bmesh.ops.scale(bm, vec=size, verts=bm.verts)\n    me = bpy.data.meshes.new(name)\n    bm.to_mesh(me)\n    bm.free()\n    ob = bpy.data.objects.new(name, me)\n    COLL.objects.link(ob)\n    ob.location = center\n    ob.rotation_euler = (0, 0, rot_z)\n    me.materials.append(mat)\n    return ob"}}]}
